# Digests of the contract binaries built for the last release.
#
# These are build outputs, not sources: they live under `target/`, which is
# ignored by git, so they cannot be part of the committed integrity manifest
# and CI cannot verify them on a clean checkout. They are recorded here
# instead, and verified against a local release build:
#
#   cargo build -p por-verifier --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --release
#   sha256sum -c audit/RELEASE_WASM.sha256
#
# A compiler update changes these bytes, so the digests are pinned to the
# release they shipped in and are refreshed deliberately — the same way a
# release manifest is. The sources that produce them are sealed by the
# committed `INTEGRITY_MANIFEST.sha256`; the audit trail for the shipped
# binary is `docs/AUDIT-EVIDENCE.md`.
#
# `por_verifier.optimized.wasm` is the size-reduced binary that was uploaded
# to the testnet contract; `por_verifier.wasm` is the plain release build of
# the same crate.
289413140b24c3d41d49dff6cd1a783d273779a1da066f2a2c2583814bba002c *target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/por_verifier.wasm
2cd7312c841372b7d9c019ad3b164883701851f000f83325e5d345e9bcf14948 *target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/por_verifier.optimized.wasm
